  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_042, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion in the multiprofile setting. All completed multimodal experiments have exclusively used imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder, so the effect of the image encoder choice in the high-performing multiprofile regime is completely untested. Question: config_049 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) changes only the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l to resnet50, making it a clean single-variable comparison against config_042. This isolates whether the ViT-L backbone is essential or whether a simpler CNN (resnet50) could match or exceed it. Why this is the best use of the next budget: The image encoder is a major architectural decision that has been held constant across all 8 experiments. Under a limited budget, resolving whether this choice matters (and in which direction) is more informative than, e.g., re-testing fusion (weighted vs concat showed only ~0.004 difference) or testing a clearly inferior RNA encoder (scgpt was ~0.10 worse than scvi_n200 in singleprofile). A large gap would confirm imagenet_vit_l is critical; a small gap would free the search to focus on other axes."
}

